	SAY NAME1 SAY NAME1 "Gauntlets"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Gauntlets are armored gloves. They can be made of leather, metal plates, or chain mail. Every suit of armor is assumed to include gauntlets of an appropriate type. Magical gauntlets tend to be finer, lighter, and more easily worn than normal varieties.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Gauntlets of the Duellist"
	SAY DESC "Designed specifically for the art of single combat, these supple leather gloves feature reinforced steel plates along the back of the hands and fingers. They are engineered to help a fighter parry swift rapier thrusts and sudden sword slashes without sacrificing grip or flexibility. For a skilled duellist, these gauntlets act as a secondary shield, easily turning a lethal strike into a harmless glance.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Armor Class: +2 vs. slashing and piercing attacks

Weight: 2"





GLOVES OF HEALING - 6500mo - solo paladini e chierici buoni //
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BRAC20.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 SAY NAME1 "Gauntlets"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "Gauntlets are armored gloves. They can be made of leather, metal plates, or chain mail. Every suit of armor is assumed to include gauntlets of an appropriate type. Magical gauntlets tend to be finer, lighter, and more easily worn than normal varieties.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2"

	SAY NAME2 "Gloves of Healing"
	SAY DESC "These gloves are crafted for anointed members of the Most Noble Order of the Radiant Heart, serving as a reliable aid during long crusades. Woven with threads blessed in the High Hall, they allow a warrior of the Light to call upon a powerful miracle of restoration when all other spells have failed. To ensure this blessing is never twisted by evil, the gloves are bound by a strict divine ward. They will remain inert and useless for anyone who does not walk the path of a righteous cleric or a devoted paladin.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1

Charge abilities:
– Cast Heal once per day

Weight: 2"





